{"body":{"text":["That a card is an anchor to the page's address the author holds wrong: \"the card being a link is wrong, a crd is just a card, navigation is external to what ever system builds it, our system is at the core nvaigation agnostic, the reader is one first example\" (23/21; 23/7). An href may still live in a Link component of the pilot's, tied to the reader (23/9). A URL and the reader's collation are the same thing to him, the URL \"just a state mechanism\" (23/29). How a press on a holon reaches what navigates is open: readers in a split pane may not use the URL, or use different q's, and since the layout is a holarchy of locations, clickability could be at that level (23/19); running a defined program for navigation is one clear way, though how it reaches everything clickable is \"still a mystery\" (23/19). Prop drilling, a component catching clicks bubbling from nodes others drew, which he holds already settled as an antipattern, and proposing by an argument's position were let go (23/11, 23/13, 23/17); an offer from the root he doubts: \"it doesnt feel right\" (23/17). For glass matches by type, never by order: \"we dont work with arguments in their order, only thourgh type matching it is a set not a list of arguments\" (23/17), so io.propose, which names what it changes by its index, owes a change. And where a component in code draws a holon in its own markup, as Value draws a card, the chassis cannot know it, where layout as data hides nothing: \"with layout as data, that's not a problem\" (23/33). *Leaning, 23/21; open: the threads Navigation outside what draws, Propose by type, not position and Holons drawn inside components in code.*"]},"id":"1M88XCXJ0KSG000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Input is to be reserved at the root, which may \"set the rules of the game\" (23/27), as OpenLight's input floor reserved its gestures, and otherwise to be the components': \"at the root, reserve gestures, etc. Otherwise, it's for the components\" (23/29). Unlike the bubbling let go above, which is a component catching what others drew, a gesture is to be passed by the chassis up the holarchy of drawings until something captures it: \"user input propagating until captures is something we need\" (23/23), the same movements expected in a Rust app as on the web (23/25). Whether the passing is ever stopped the author does not know (23/27); of a button, \"pressing a button is pressing a button. Nothing's to be propagated there\", though \"I can't say for sure that that's a golden rule\" (23/31). Right-click is so reserved for the context menu, which is given where it was pressed in the holarchy and does the rest by matching: \"It's all just pure matching\" (23/29). Above the content an overlay layer is to stand, the completion menu and the context menu its first: \"I think we should do layers and the overlay system\" (23/29). *Leaning, 23/23 to 23/29; open: the threads Input reserved at the root, propagated until captured, The context menu as matching over the holarchy and Layers and overlays.*"]},"id":"1M88XCXJ0KSG001","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Beside them, open. Chrome is no component's to implement, whose it is unknown, and a focus ring is chrome too (23/29, 23/31). Chassis of many kinds are to nest, DOM and canvas, and a node view of the interface's own holarchy is wanted soon, as a global action (23/27, 23/29). Keys and accessibility are the system's to define, their data probably shipped with the field; what implements them \"might be up to the chassis, or might be a decoupled piece from the chassis. I don't know exactly\" (23/29), and \"I don't know if ARIA roles are enough\" (23/31). *Open: the threads Chrome around nested components, Chassis of many kinds, nested, and Accessibility and keys defined by the system.*"]},"id":"1M88XCXJ0KSG002","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Agents briefed narrowly fail that freedom. In the twenty-third session four were sent with one brief of the session's own framing, each started from a topic; the author did not know how informed they were and trusted the process little: \"this wasn't a particularly intelligent way of running agents either\" (23/31). The session conceded they argued its framing, one read Knowledge only in part, none had the conversation, and their agreement was one opinion counted four times (23/32). Agents are to bootstrap themselves from the field: \"they all ought to explore without constraints, and they all ought to have a certain culture of exploration, of critique, and digestion\" (23/35). Whether they are steered, siloed by topic, or first talk among themselves he does not know; \"So maybe we send off 3 just completely free to explore everything within there\" (23/35). *Open: the thread Free agents and their orchestration.*"]},"id":"1M88XCXJ0KSG003","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}